n    map.on('click', function() {\\n      layers.forEach(function(layer) { layer.setStyle({color: '#555555', weight: 0.6, fillOpacity: 0.85}); });\\n    });\\n  }).call(this.getMap(), el, x, data);\\n}\",\"data\":[{\"pin10\":\"0734207020\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734207022\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734400002\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734400003\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734400020\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734400030\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734400031\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734400032\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734401072\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734402018\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734402020\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734402025\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734402033\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734402034\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0734402035\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735200005\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735316002\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735316003\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735400008\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735400009\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735400011\",\"keypins\":\"\"},{\"pin10\":\"0735400034\",\"keypins\":\"\"}]}]}}</script>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## Explore Projects in Roselle with multiple PINs\n\nClick a footprint to highlight the footprints sharing its key PINs; click the blank map background to reset. Only projects with at least two PINs **within this region** are included. Counts include unmapped PINs; shared footprints can belong to more than one project. Gray indicates a footprint shared by multiple displayed projects. \n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<p>No multi-PIN projects with usable 2024 parcel geometry are available.</p>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n\n## Roselle Property Overview\n\nThese counts cover distinct fourteen-digit PINs in the historical commercial/industrial universe (2006–2024). Status and parcel geometry are from **2024**. Region membership uses the universe's latest available geographic assignment; this is not a historical boundary analysis.\n\n\n\n::: {#tbl-region-overview .cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|Measure                                     | Count|\n|:-------------------------------------------|-----:|\n|Historical C&I PINs (2006-2024 universe)    |    22|\n|Observed in 2024                            |    22|\n|Exempt in 2024 (class 0)                    |     1|\n|Incentive PINs (2024 classes 600-899)       |     0|\n|PINs in a TIF (2024 membership)             |    13|\n|Unknown 2024 class                          |     0|\n|Not observed in 2024                        |     0|\n|Assigned projects                           |     0|\n|Projects with multiple PINs in this region  |     0|\n|PINs without a project assignment           |    22|\n|Mapped ten-digit footprints (2024 geometry) |    22|\n|PINs without usable 2024 geometry           |     0|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nOf the 22 PINs observed in 2024, **1 are class 0** (4.5%).\n\n## What types of property are these PINs in 2024?\n\nThis table counts individual PINs by their **2024 assessor property classification**, with the class description beside each code. It does not count projects: one project can contain PINs in several classes. Because the sample includes properties that were commercial or industrial in earlier years, residential, vacant, and exempt classes can also appear. The final missing-record category has no known 2024 classification.\n\n\n::: {#tbl-class-summary .cell tbl-cap='PIN counts by 2024 property class'}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n\n|2024 class |Description                                                                        | PINs|\n|:----------|:----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----:|\n|0          |Exempt or Railroad property                                                        |    1|\n|190        |Minor improvement on vacant land, Other minor improvement which does not add value |    3|\n|517        |One-story commercial building                                                      |    6|\n|522        |One-story, non-fireproof public garage                                             |    2|\n|523        |Gasoline station                                                                   |    1|\n|531        |Shopping center                                                                    |    5|\n|590        |Commercial minor improvement                                                       |    1|\n|592        |Two-or-three-story building containing part or all retail and/or commercial space  |    2|\n|597        |Special commercial structure                                                       |    1|\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Projects in Roselle\n\nCounts and values include only PINs within this region. A project may extend into another region, so regional project counts are not additive. Unassigned PINs are excluded from project totals. FMV means estimated fair market value. Incentive PINs are 2024 classes 600-899. FMV is summed only over known 2024 values; an entirely missing valuation remains missing. The project identifier uses Appellant, falling back to Key PIN. Last Year of Paid Taxbill lists each distinct latest year in which a PIN had a bill greater than $0 during 2006-2024; it does not confirm payment. PINs without a positive bill in that history are identified separately. TIF counts use 2024 PIN-to-TIF membership records regardless of payment or increment, rather than positive distributions. Missing 2024 records are not counted as known TIF members.\n\n\n::: {#tbl-projects .cell .column-screen-inset tbl-cap='Projects, appellants, and 2024 values'}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-ad0c69ee713022319d29\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;\" class=\"datatables html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-ad0c69ee713022319d29\">{\"x\":{\"filter\":\"top\",\"ver